 "capsule": "The Iraqi Republic was constituted after the 14 July 1958 coup that overthrew Iraq's Hashemite monarchy, and its early republican decade under Abd al-Karim Qasim (1958-63) gave way to Ba'athist and Arab-nationalist governments after further coups in 1963 and 1968, entrenching Ahmad Hasan al-Bakr and then Saddam Hussein in power. The republic was convulsed by the Iran-Iraq War (1980-88), the 1990 invasion of Kuwait, and UN sanctions before the March 2003 U.S.-led invasion toppled Saddam's government; a Coalition-administered transition then produced a new permanent constitution in October 2005 and a fresh government taking office in 2006.",
 "citations": [
